{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#|grab|cursor|ring|rail|platform|control'\"' legs_log.md\"","aggregated_output":"1:# Leg-library debrief log\n3:Recurring composition patterns and repeated novelty.\n5:## Level 1: switchable platforms (verified)\n6:- Public clone probes identify color 14 as the avatar: keys 1/2/3/4 move it by two pixels up/down/left/right on connected colored platforms. From pristine entry, repeated up stops at (row 38, col 10) until the lower bridge moves.\n8:- Verified subgoals: lower bridge -> red platform at (30,10) -> purple platform at (30,20) -> upper bridge at (24,20) -> destination color 11 at (20,24). The lower button must be toggled back after crossing it to restore the final connection.\n12:## Level 3: revealed switch and paired transport (verified clone probes)\n14:- probe_mechanics.py reproduces both reversible bridge controls from entry and multiple avatar positions: (52,18) exchanges horizontal color-8 spans for vertical spans; (52,27) exchanges the left horizontal color-9 connection for three other connections.\n19:- Reuse: play_level_3 composes navigate_switchable_platforms to waypoint (42,16), then to the reward, adding the newly revealed switch only for the second stage. No new leg is needed. A direct goal search and a second-stage search without the revealed button both exhausted their bounds; clone observations falsified the missing-button assumption before the corrected player was tested.\n22:## Level 3: recovered verified path artifact\n26:## Level 4: recovered verified path artifact\n30:## Level 5: hand-controlled platform and cyclic bridges\n32:- `probe_grab.py` verifies that up three/right three presses bring the hand beside the color-12 platform; (52,35) grips it, and subsequent hand directions relocate it in four-pixel steps around the black corridor.\n33:- `probe_ride.py` and `probe_rider_detail.py` falsify automatic riding: dragging is blocked while the walker occupies the platform. `probe_stage.py` verifies bridging to the middle island (20,26), parking the walker there, returning the platform, and climbing to (6,22).\n34:- `probe_portal.py` verifies that walking to (6,24) then pressing (52,48) transports the walker to (34,10). Dragging the platform left three/down three now connects this portal to the isolated pickup at (18,10); `probe_pickup_left.py` verifies collection and the revealed pink button at (52,14).\n35:- `probe_finish.py` verifies four presses of each cyclic control (56,22) and (47,22), plus the revealed pink switch. Crossing the extended horizontal bridge, descending the right pink bridge, and restoring the left pink bridge reaches the color-11 goal and increments the clone reward to 5.\n36:- Dense progress is staged island/pickup reachability and Manhattan distance for the existing navigation leg. New `manipulate_platform_controls` verifies each drag or cyclic-control press on a clone before committing. Level 5 only composes these two legs.\n40:## Level 5: recovered verified path artifact\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
